# Drafted by Gemini (R24 grove), edited.

~ grove_start
Narrator: The crooked pines knit their boughs together behind your backs with a sound like dry knuckles cracking. Ahead, in an all too neat circle of trunks, pale women in white linen kneel in the black loam, scratching at the roots.
set ct_grove_started
-> END

~ rowan
ct_false_rowan [afraid]: Please, you have hands that haven't bled yet, come help me dig. My name is Rowan, and I've dropped my gold locket down among the roots where the dark takes everything.
* [Insight DC 18] See through her -> rowan_seen | rowan_f
* Listen to her tale -> rowan_tale
* Walk past, out of reach -> rowan_pass
* Step closer -> rowan_close

~ rowan_seen
Narrator: Her chest never rises, and her dirt-caked fingers move in time with the slow, sap-heavy creak of the trunk behind her. The girl is only a soft bait dangling from a very hungry fishing line.
-> rowan

~ rowan_f
Narrator: A single tear tracks through the peat on her cheek, and she shivers with a cold that looks entirely human.
ct_false_rowan [sad]: It has her hair inside it, braided with mine. Don't leave me digging in the cold alone.
-> rowan

~ rowan_tale
ct_false_rowan [sad]: Once I was the Green Queen's dearest heart, before she learned how mortal love turns sour in the mouth. Everything she cherished became the knife that carved her, and still I kept her token.
ct_false_rowan [smile]: It's just under this root, I swear it. Give me your warm hand and pull.
-> rowan

~ rowan_pass
Narrator: You keep a wide berth of the white hem and the waiting roots, though her head turns after you further than a neck ought to go.
-> END

~ rowan_close
ct_false_rowan [angry]: Too close, sweet meat. The boughs have been thirsty all night.
Narrator: The pale face splits down the seam of the nose like wet bark, and the great timber behind her uncurls its limbs.
combat ct_maidenwood

~ centre
if flag.ct_maidenwood_done
-> centre_clear
endif
Narrator: The turf in the middle of the ring smells of crushed lily and sweet rot, and a low hum tugs at the back of your teeth, bidding you go comfort the weeping girls.
* Cross the centre, quickly -> centre_cross
* Go round the edge, out of the centre -> centre_edge
* Back off -> END

~ centre_cross
Narrator: You set your boots onto the mossy heart of the ring, where the air hangs thick as honey.
check Wisdom DC 16 -> centre_ok | centre_charmed

~ centre_edge
Narrator: You pick your way between the outer stones and the reach of the weeping figures, slow and careful, where the sweet hum is only a draught in the pines.
-> centre_clear

~ centre_ok
Narrator: The sorrow in the soil tugs at your sleeves like a child begging, but you keep your eyes on the northern trees and walk on through.
-> centre_clear

~ centre_charmed
Narrator: {name}'s eyes go glassy with borrowed grief, feet already drifting toward the nearest white gown and the roots that wait behind her.
ct_false_rowan [sly]: That's it, darling. Lay your head right down in the loam.
damage 1d10 psychic
combat ct_maidenwood

~ centre_clear
Narrator: On the north side of the ring, the braided branches groan and part around a narrow goat track climbing into the dark.
set ct_grove_done
quest the_crooked_tree tracking_phillip
-> END
